the iron chain (over the left shoulder, held in the left hand at the chest, running back to the pot), the big pot and its wooden cart (built as a separate prop asset), any glow, smoke, embers or bloom; the concept's deep hunch with the head sunk low between the shoulders and in front of the chest, and its wide-legged stance. Hands empty and open. Hands empty and open. No other loose props.
Asymmetric details stay on the same body side in every view: In the concept the chain lies over the LEFT shoulder and the LEFT hand holds it at the chest; both are removed, so the body is symmetric: the scarf V, the cloak, the apron and the robe panels hang centred and even on both sides. LEFT view: the figure's own left side toward the camera, facing screen-left; RIGHT view: its right side, facing screen-right.
No text, labels, numbers, logo, watermark or scenery. No human silhouette.

VIEWS: Heights are % of the figure height (0 % = the top of the centre brick, 100 % = soles), the SAME in every view. BRICK CROWN 0-13 % (FRONT: the seven bricks fanned with the tallest in the middle; BACK: the same ring from behind, the shorter rear bricks in front of the taller front ones; LEFT and RIGHT: the ring in profile, the tallest brick at the front). IRON BAND 13-16 %. FACE GUARD 15-22 % (FRONT only; LEFT and RIGHT: its edge at the front of the head; BACK: the back of the linen-wrapped head under the band). CHIN WRAP 22-27 %. SCARF COWL round the neck 22-34 %, its V on the chest down to about 45 % (FRONT; LEFT and RIGHT: a thick roll round the neck in profile; BACK: a thick roll across the top of the cloak at 24-32 %). SHOULDERS AND ARMS at about 30 %, arms horizontal, hands at 30-32 %; in LEFT and RIGHT the near hand points at the camera at about 30 % in front of the chest. CLOAK: over both shoulders from about 26 %; in BACK it covers the whole back down to big jagged points at about 62 %; in FRONT only its two side edges hang at the sides of the torso behind the arms down to about 55 % and the cowl and apron show between them; in LEFT and RIGHT it humps over the back and hangs to about 62 % at the back edge; it never covers the arms (the arms come out from under it). APRON 32-85 % at the front (FRONT; the front edge in LEFT and RIGHT; hidden in BACK). RED-BROWN ROBE at the sides and back from under the cloak to jagged points at about 85 % (BACK shows it below the cloak, 62-85 %). DARK UNDERSKIRT 82-90 % all round. WRAPPED SHINS 88-96 %, FEET 96-100 %. LEGS: two short identical legs side by side in FRONT and BACK; in LEFT and RIGHT one leg hides the other.
Asset-specific PROPORTIONS override generic humanoid ratios. Preserve short legs and crown. Side silhouette broad swollen belly, rounded upper back, head above shoulders. Match the selected front/back as closely as possible.


